Enlightenment:
int something(Sensor &s){
return s.read();
}
```
adding the inherited "child" class as a parameter in your main code would make the compiler be like "i see, you called a class that inherited this certain thing from another class. imma copy the function from that class instead".
Virtual functions are for when you want to just accept data. Irrespective of which class it comes from. You want to be able to accept the read function irrespective of if it comes from the mpu class or another sensor class and use it to do cool stuff.

